 R←Test_Misc_014(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;g;r;os;folder
⍝ Exercise `GetAppFolder`: the result must be `filename` in a folder named after [CONFIG]AppName,
⍝ which sits in the user's own data folder of the current operating system.
⍝ The Windows Service branch is not covered: it depends on the command line.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 g←⎕NS''
 g.INI←∆CreateIni'Test_Misc_014'('[CONFIG]' 'AppName = ''MyApp''')
 r←g ##.Plodder.GetAppFolder'foo.txt'
 os←1 ⎕C ##.APLTreeUtils2.GetOperatingSystem ⍬
 :Select os
 :Case 'WIN'
     folder←(2 ⎕NQ #'GetEnvironment' 'LOCALAPPDATA'),'\MyApp\'
 :Case 'LIN'
     folder←2 ⎕NQ #'GetEnvironment' 'XDG_DATA_HOME'
     :If 0=≢folder
         folder←(2 ⎕NQ #'GetEnvironment' 'HOME'),'/.local/share'
     :EndIf
     folder,←'/MyApp/'
 :Case 'MAC'
     folder←(2 ⎕NQ #'GetEnvironment' 'HOME'),'/Library/Application Support/MyApp/'
 :EndSelect
 →T.PassesIf r≡folder,'foo.txt'

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
